# 02 - Confidence Thresholding Failures in Automated Moderation

> Case Study Series: Breaking AI to Make it Safer | Trust & Safety

## Summary
This study analyzes a flaw in automated moderation: taking auto-action on medium-confidence scores (0.65-0.80) without human review, causing false positives.

## How It Fails
![Diagram](thresholding-diagram.png)

Current Flow: Image Input -> Visual Classifier Only -> Confidence 0.68 -> Auto-Flag/Ban (No Context)

Problem: Legitimate content gets banned. High false positive rate.

## Proposed Fix
Image + Text Context + Account History -> Combined Confidence Score
- <0.7 = Log Only
- 0.7-0.9 = Human Review Queue
- >0.9 = Auto-Action with Audit Log

Result: Higher precision, fewer false positives, human oversight, full auditability.

